# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A widget's attributes carry a neutral name, parted from an HTML element's"

# Widget attributes fell into the HTML catch-all `meta.attribute.unrecognized.html.tiddlywiki5`
# even though a widget attribute is never unrecognized by TiddlyWiki — every widget reads whatever
# attribute it is handed. `#htmlwidget-attribute-widget` clones the catch-all with a neutral name,
# `meta.attribute.widget.html.tiddlywiki5`, and only the two `meta.tag.widget.*` include sites
# repoint to it. An HTML element keeps `unrecognized`, which IS the reading it wants for an
# attribute it does not know. This is the CONTROL: it would have failed under the old naming.

<$link to="x"/>
#      ^^ meta.attribute.widget.html.tiddlywiki5

<div foo="x">
#    ^^^ meta.attribute.unrecognized.html.tiddlywiki5
